2. Staff whose sick leave exceeds two months shall, from the third month, be paid salary during sick leave according to the following standards:
(1) If the length of service is less than ten years, 90% of their salary shall be paid;
(2) If the length of service is ten years or more, their full salary shall be paid.

3. Staff whose sick leave exceeds six months shall, from the seventh month, be paid salary during sick leave according to the following standards:
(1) If the length of service is less than ten years, 70% of their salary shall be paid;
(2) If the length of service is ten years or more, 80% of their salary shall be paid;
(3) For staff who participated in revolutionary work before September 2, 1945, 90% of their salary shall be paid.
Among the staff mentioned in items (1), (2), and (3) above, those who have been conferred the titles of labor hero or labor model by the people's governments of provinces, municipalities directly under the Central Government, and autonomous regions, or by various departments of the State Council, and still maintain the honor, may, subject to approval by the people's governments of provinces, municipalities directly under the Central Government, and autonomous regions, or by various departments of the State Council, have their salary during sick leave appropriately increased.
